Ran 7 tests across 1 file. [20.00ms]
```

Decisions the request did not spell out:
- Blank line = empty or whitespace-only; runs of blank lines collapse to one separator; leading/trailing blank lines are dropped (so `""` / `"\n\n"` return `""`).
- Input split on `/\r?\n/` so CRLF works; within a paragraph newlines act as a single space.
- `width` is floored (`5.9` behaves as `5`); the `RangeError` check is `!(width >= 1)`, so `NaN` also throws.
- A split long word's last chunk stays on the current line, so a following short word can join it if it fits (e.g. `wrap("hi abcdefgh bye", 3)` → `"hi\nabc\ndef\ngh\nbye"`).

